p on github so if  you have any questions please let me  know but  you can see there's just like a list of  police beat numbers  list of months and you cycle through  them  pulling from blast and then  cycle through the list of urls pulling  everything from the span tag  if the formatting was different so utf-8  versus unicode i used  the unicode decode error also requests  to check for 404's  csv for being able to append to an  output csv  file a beautiful soup for the for the  web scraping  and was since they're all tables with  again the same format  um it was really pretty simple to do  that  and then anything with the same column  name  you just check for column name and sort  of move it around  so the results i got a final output csv  with just under a million criminal  offenses  in houston from june 2009 to february  2015. and these aren't  criminal offenses like hey i saw my best  friend  smoking marijuana in his dorm room it's  all like hey  i you know this is a murder this is an  aggravated assault this is a burglary  this is a theft like these are pretty  severe crimes  and they're now divided into city blocks  with standard formats for  columns and block names so things that  you can actually use in a gis capacity  they're compatible with the city of  houston's enterprise roads  shapefile and if anyone was curious my  district  is responsible for 5.125  of the total crimes despite only housing  4 of the population and covering 18  miles  so it's that really really tiny pink  block  that you see sort of in the center of  houston  so um what am i going to  do with the data now like we've got i've  gotten to the part  of i've obtained it it's a pretty  substantial file  should probably end up being a data  frame or some sort of  database that i house  and also i would really like to do this  for the majority of houston so if  someone  really does have that question like  where should i park my car on west timer  what's the safest drop for me to get to  work they would be able to answer that  without having to use arcgis and do the  network analyst tool  so next steps i would like to  incorporate the 311 data  which is noise complaints garbage and  yards water sewage outages and they  still have  the the terrible monthly download by  district  csv format so ripe for web scraping  and then putting everything online with  an open source gis  so people are able to query crime rates  for given blocks  and route them around potentially  dangerous  areas so  thanks to a lot of people but  particularly  the node co-working space they let me  hang out yesterday and  i think a couple of people from there  are actually here this afternoon  open houston which is responsible for  even putting  any of the data online for me to have  access to  and also my earth science classmates for  asking the questions that made me do  this project in the first place  so there you go

